    <string name="step_install_termux">Step 1: Install Termux</string>
    <string name="btn_install_termux">Install Termux from F-Droid</string>
    <string name="btn_installed_continue">I\'ve installed it — continue</string>
    <string name="termux_install_body">Vibe Tavern needs Termux to run the local server on your device.\n\nIMPORTANT: install Termux from F-Droid, not the Play Store. The Play Store version is outdated and will not work.</string>

    <string name="step_grant_permission">Step 2: Grant Permission</string>
    <string name="btn_open_settings">Open Vibe Tavern Settings</string>
    <string name="btn_continue">Continue</string>
    <string name="permission_guide_body">This permission belongs to Vibe Tavern, not Termux.\n\nFirst run this in Termux:\n  mkdir -p ~/.termux\n  echo &quot;allow-external-apps=true&quot; &gt;&gt; ~/.termux/termux.properties\n\nIf termux-reload-settings crashes, force stop Termux and open it again.\n\nThen:\n1. Open Vibe Tavern settings below\n2. Use ⋮ → &quot;Allow restricted settings&quot;\n3. Open Permissions → ⋮ → &quot;All permissions&quot;\n4. Enable &quot;Run commands in Termux environment&quot;\n5. Return here and tap Continue</string>

